From a48d47903a35d08f6df833d97097030cbd01a756 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:10:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] arm64: dts: qcom: agatti: fix the GIC maintenance
 interrupt

The GIC node lists PPI 9 (INTID 25) as the maintenance interrupt, but
the Agatti interrupt map routes the CPU interface maintenance output
(nVCPUMNTIRQ) to PPI 8 (INTID 24); INTID 25 is the wakeup sync line.
KVM's vGIC therefore never sees a maintenance interrupt, and the Arm
BSA PPI check times out on a QRB2210 board at EL2:

  Interrupt not received within timeout
  Failed at checkpoint -  4

With PPI 8 the same check receives it.

Fixes: a64a0192b70c ("arm64: dts: qcom: Add initial QCM2290 device tree")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/agatti.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/agatti.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/agatti.dtsi
index 75cbfabf1..cb8dcda8c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/agatti.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/agatti.dtsi
@@ -2787,7 +2787,7 @@ intc: interrupt-controller@f200000 {
 			compatible = "arm,gic-v3";
 			reg = <0x0 0x0f200000 0x0 0x10000>,
 			      <0x0 0x0f300000 0x0 0x100000>;
-			interrupts = <GIC_PPI 9 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_PPI 8 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			#interrupt-cells = <3>;
 			interrupt-controller;
 			interrupt-parent = <&intc>;
-- 
